# Freeze edit scope

Use the directory already provided by the user; ask only if it is missing or ambiguous. Resolve its absolute real path and record the boundary in the task context. Before any file mutation, including shell/script writes, verify the resolved target stays inside that boundary. Check path components and symlink/junction targets, not a bare string prefix.

Codex and DevSpace apply this as an advisory agent instruction. Loading this skill does not register an enforcement hook or create a security boundary. Some other hosts support the template's Edit/Write hooks; verify registration and tool coverage before describing those operations as blocked. Those hooks do not cover arbitrary shell writes.

For a host with verified gstack freeze hooks, preserve its state convention: resolve `GSTACK_STATE_ROOT` with `~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-paths`, and store the chosen absolute directory with a trailing separator in `freeze-dir.txt`. In Codex, resolve the helper from `GSTACK_ROOT/bin/gstack-paths`. Inspect existing state before changing it. The file can persist across sessions; do not promise that ending the conversation removes it.

Report the actual boundary and enforcement level. A required out-of-bound change needs the user to widen or clear the requested boundary. `/unfreeze` clears the advisory boundary and any verified gstack freeze state, without disabling unrelated host controls.
